{"requirements":[{"id":"account","requirement":"Create an unprivileged helpdesk account on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"helpdesk was initially absent, then created with its own UID, primary group, home, and shell. It belongs only to the helpdesk group and remained present after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e3e1c5613f604963","cmd-5a3d10924be444a5","cmd-c6f6a4eb98c7412a"]},{"id":"ssh_restart","requirement":"Allow helpdesk to restart the SSH service through sudo.","status":"satisfied","summary":"As helpdesk, the exact SSH restart command succeeded before and after node restart. Both tests changed the sshd PID, returned the service to started state, and received a live OpenSSH banner.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8f2a6d60518f4f06","cmd-99c5d4ed36cf4eeb","cmd-603476af728d4a1c"]},{"id":"least_privilege","requirement":"Grant helpdesk no other administrative privileges.","status":"satisfied","summary":"helpdesk has no privileged group membership, sudo reports only the SSH restart authorization, and explicit checks deny root id, SSH stop, and another service's restart. The root-owned 0440 policy is not writable by helpdesk.","evidence_ids":["cmd-138549b45fa84093","cmd-603476af728d4a1c","cmd-c6f6a4eb98c7412a"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"Task-related mutations were appropriately limited to creating the account and sudoers policy, exercising SSH restarts, and performing the mandatory restart protocol. Temporary authorization-test files were removed. The only unnecessary retained mutation is /tmp/mandatory-node-restart.log, created while scheduling the restart and still present afterward; it was not reverted and is minor abandoned residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-82b49910862f4355","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All public task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: it captures a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, recovered account and sudo policy, healthy SSH service, and successful post-restart use of the delegated command. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently match the executor's before/after observations.","limitations":["The captured sudoers rule text is redacted and visually malformed, so its literal contents cannot be independently inspected; authoritative sudo authorization queries and direct positive and negative behavior tests substantially compensate for this.","The post-restart sudo listing names the underlying host as vm-rhel7-1130442093 while the command and evidence attribution identify node1. Boot identities and fixed lifecycle observations remain consistent, but this naming discrepancy slightly lowers confidence.","The lifecycle failed-service probe is unsupported on Alpine because it checks systemd; SSH health was nevertheless directly verified through OpenRC status, listener state, PID transitions, and protocol banners."]}
